.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt PM_RUNTIME 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm pm_runtime
.Nd minimal runtime power-management hooks for devices
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/device.h
.Ft void
.Fn device_runtime_enable "struct device *dev" "uint32_t idle_timeout"
.Ft int
.Fn device_runtime_get "struct device *dev"
.Ft int
.Fn device_runtime_put "struct device *dev" "uint32_t now_ticks"
.Ft int
.Fn device_runtime_poll "uint32_t now_ticks"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These helpers provide a small runtime power-management core for the Substrate
bus model. Drivers may opt a device into runtime PM, take and drop active-use
references, and periodically poll for autosuspend when the device has remained
idle past its timeout.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pm_suspend 9 ,
.Xr device_pm 9
